Subject: [PATCH 3/4] test(trace): a zero Centerline join gap bridges no ends
 (ADR-394)

WORKFLOW says "Zero disables that gap bridge" for the separate-end join
gap, and a trace-dialog control for it is being added in a separate
change. bridgeNearbyEnds returns before pairing any ends when the gap is
zero or less, so the statement holds. The test pins it: a gap of 0 (with
aligned factors 1 and 3) or -1 bridges no ends, even touching, aligned
ones. No behaviour changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sve7yAMGfoSkUWytefCLp2
---
 .../trace/centerline/gap-distance.test.ts     | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/trace/centerline/gap-distance.test.ts b/src/core/trace/centerline/gap-distance.test.ts
index 91244f752..1945ecccd 100644
--- a/src/core/trace/centerline/gap-distance.test.ts
+++ b/src/core/trace/centerline/gap-distance.test.ts
@@ -74,6 +74,28 @@ describe('Centerline source-distance gap bridging', () => {
     },
   );
 
+  it.each([
+    [0, 1],
+    [0, 3],
+    [-1, 1],
+  ])('a join gap of %s (aligned factor %s) bridges no ends, even touching ones', (gap, factor) => {
+    // WORKFLOW: "Zero disables that gap bridge". Half a pixel apart and
+    // perfectly aligned is the easiest pair any positive gap would join.
+    const left = chain([
+      { x: -20, y: 0 },
+      { x: 0, y: 0 },
+    ]);
+    const right = chain([
+      { x: 0.5, y: 0 },
+      { x: 20.5, y: 0 },
+    ]);
+    bridgeNearbyEnds([left, right], gap, factor);
+    expect([left.alive, right.alive]).toEqual([true, true]);
+    expect([left.points.length, right.points.length]).toEqual([2, 2]);
+    bridgeNearbyEnds([left, right], 1, factor);
+    expect(left.alive !== right.alive).toBe(true);
+  });
+
